      "replacements": [
        [
          "This work-only group recycle candidate supplements the preserved entry/history epochs with recursive group list/preview, confirmed recycle/purge and valid previous-parent restoration. It is not installed in production.",
          "Group list/preview, confirmed recursive recycle/purge and valid previous-parent restoration supplement the preserved entry/history workflows."
        ],
        [
          "history comparison/deletion/settings/age cleanup; group recycling/recovery and whole-bin emptying; group rename/reordering/management UI;",
          "history comparison/deletion/settings/age cleanup; whole-bin emptying; general group rename/reordering/management UI;"
        ],
        [
          "Root will add current production-source results after installation; this proposal makes no new behavioral pass claim. Group recovery, empty bin, multi-selection and complete KeePass parity remain open.",
          "Those entry epochs retain their original sources and counts. Recursive group recovery is described in [GROUP-RECYCLE.md](GROUP-RECYCLE.md), with the [immutable group evidence map](../../results/vault-group-recycle-reviewed-installation-20261013/source-proof/preservation-manifest.json). Whole-bin emptying, multi-selection, general group management and complete KeePass parity remain open.\n\nThe final guarded candidate passed77 focused checks. The independent root replay passed the exact six previously tested case bodies, including the formerly failing held active-list case. A separate real shared-host HTTP campaign passed two cases through five process starts, including four recycle/restore/purge restarts, native tombstone order, history and encrypted-record checks. A normal shared Studio host and shell additionally passed eight finite browser observations for preview, confirmation, recycling, password reveal, recursive restoration, preview clearing and empty-bin reopening. These are distinct campaigns, not a combined test denominator. Original GUI/full-program executions and timing/resource comparative acceptance remain zero. The original15 managed-load author campaign remains its immutable initial777 epoch; it is not rebound to the corrected client. Current installed-source focused checks are recorded separately after installation."
        ]
